          }
        },
        "qa_pb_01": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-basics",
            "question": "What is the difference between APGO coating and traditional waxing?",
            "answer": "<p>APGO coating forms a more stable protective layer on the surface, while traditional wax mainly provides short-term gloss. With regular maintenance, APGO coating offers better water repellency, easier cleaning, and stronger resistance to environmental contaminants.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_pb_02": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-basics",
            "question": "Which exterior surfaces can APGO coating be used on?",
            "answer": "<p>APGO coating is suitable for painted panels, glass, plastic trims, rubber trims, and chrome parts on the exterior. For safety reasons, please avoid applying coating directly on tire tread surfaces.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_pb_03": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-basics",
            "question": "How many times can one bottle be used?",
            "answer": "<p>As a general guideline, one bottle can be used approximately 8-10 times, depending on vehicle size, application amount, and coverage area.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_pb_04": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-basics",
            "question": "How long does APGO coating typically last?",
            "answer": "<p>Typical durability ranges from about 2 weeks to 2 months. Actual performance depends on weather exposure, parking conditions, wash frequency, and daily driving environment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "category_application_maintenance": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Application & Maintenance",
            "key": "application-maintenance"
          }
        },
        "qa_am_01": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "application-maintenance",
            "question": "How often should I apply coating?",
            "answer": "<p>For new users, we recommend applying once a week in the first month to build the base layer. Afterwards, you may adjust to once every two weeks, then once a month for maintenance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_am_02": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "application-maintenance",
            "question": "Do I need to avoid water after application?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. To achieve better bonding and durability, avoid direct water exposure for approximately 12-24 hours after application whenever possible.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_am_03": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "application-maintenance",
            "question": "Can I apply coating right after an outside car wash?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes, but we recommend rinsing once more with clean water before application. This helps remove fine dust picked up during the drive back and reduces the risk of micro-scratches.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_am_04": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "application-maintenance",
            "question": "Should coating be applied on a wet or dry surface?",
            "answer": "<p>It depends on product type. The Atomic series is designed for wet application, while dry-application ranges such as Titanium and Atomic Coloured Glaze are intended for dry surfaces.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_am_05": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "application-maintenance",
            "question": "Why do I still see some dust and water droplets after coating?",
            "answer": "<p>Dust and water cannot be fully eliminated due to static and environmental factors. Coating improves surface behavior so contaminants are less likely to stick firmly and are easier to clean during regular maintenance.</p>"
          }
        },
        "category_product_selection": {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Product Selection",
            "key": "product-selection"
          }
        },
        "qa_ps_01": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-selection",
            "question": "Which APGO coating is recommended for first-time DIY users?",
            "answer": "<p>For beginners, we usually recommend Atomic Crystal Coating or Atomic Sealing Coating because these wet-application formulas are easier to handle and provide reliable performance in daily use.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_8LkRDQ": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-selection",
            "question": "What are the main differences in the Atomic coating series?",
            "answer": "<p>Atomic Car Nano Coating (Orange): Our basic version<br/><br/>Atomic Crystal Car Nano Coating (Dark Green): Upgraded version, improved dust resistance and hydrophobicity<br/><br/>Atomic Sealing Car Nano Coating (Brown): Upgraded version, improved durability and wash resistance<br/><br/>Atomic Glaze Car Nano Coating (Light Green): Comprehensive upgrade, upgraded in all aspect<br/><br/>Atomic Aurora Coating (Light Blue): Our latest coating in the atomic series coating.  It is the strongest in the atomic coating series and has 6 stars across all functions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_ps_03": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-selection",
            "question": "What is the difference between dry-application and wet-application coatings?",
            "answer": "<p>Dry-application coatings generally deliver stronger bonding, longer durability, and deeper gloss. Wet-application coatings are faster and easier to use, making them suitable for DIY and routine upkeep.</p>"
          }
        },
        "qa_ps_04": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "category_key": "product-selection",
            "question": "What is the difference between ceramic coating and spray coating?",
            "answer": "<p>Ceramic coating creates a thicker and harder long-term layer and usually requires more preparation and skill. Spray coating is easier for DIY maintenance, forms a lighter protective layer, and can be improved through repeated applications.</p>"
          }
        },
